'' Every accepted encoding normalises to UTF-8 and reports correct byte counts.
''
'' UTF-32LE is the one that needs asserting rather than assuming: its BOM 'FF FE 00 00'
'' BEGINS WITH the UTF-16LE BOM, so a detector that tests UTF-16 first reads the whole
'' file as UTF-16LE followed by a stream of NULs -- which does not fail, it produces
'' nonsense. The two must therefore both appear here, and both decode to the same text.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-source tests/source/plain.bas tests/source/utf16le.bas tests/source/utf8bom.bas tests/source/utf32le.bas tests/source/utf32be.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' The two UTF-32 fixtures hold the SAME TEXT, so their content hashes must match -- a
'' stronger assertion than either decoding alone, since it fails if one endianness is
'' byte-swapped, truncated, or read as UTF-16.
'' EXPECT-OUT: encoding=utf-32le
'' EXPECT-OUT: encoding=utf-32be
'' GOLDEN: expected/encodings.out
